messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff-i386.c
Line: 510
Function: coff_pe_i386_relocate_section
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-122
Explanation: Writes a 16-bit value into contents at contents + (rel->r_vaddr - input_section->vma) without validating that rel->r_vaddr lies within the current section’s bounds. A malformed COFF file can set r_vaddr outside [input_section->vma, input_section->vma + input_section->size), causing an out-of-bounds write past the heap-allocated section buffer.

